# Web performance guardrails

## Budgets (fail the PR, not the build)

- Field p75: LCP ≤ 2.5 s · INP ≤ 200 ms · CLS ≤ 0.1 · TTFB ≤ 800 ms
- Initial JS per route ≤ 170 KB gz (marketing) / ≤ 300 KB gz (app)
- ≤ 3 third-party scripts on any route; none synchronous in `<head>`

## LCP rules (non-negotiable)

- The LCP image is never `loading="lazy"`; it gets `priority` (`next/image`) or `fetchpriority="high"` + preload
- LCP content is server-rendered and in the HTML — not a CSS background, not client-fetched
- Every `<img>/<video>/<iframe>` has dimensions or `aspect-ratio`

## Rendering

- Server Components by default; `'use client'` only at interactive leaves
- Slow data goes behind `<Suspense>` with a sized skeleton; never block the shell
- React Compiler is on (`reactCompiler: true`); do not hand-write `memo`/`useMemo`/`useCallback` without Profiler evidence

## Responsiveness (INP)

- No task > 50 ms in an input handler; yield with `scheduler.yield()` / `startTransition`
- No synchronous layout reads in handlers
- Third-party scripts: `<Script strategy="lazyOnload">` or consent-gated; embeds use facades

## Navigation

- No `unload` listeners (bfcache); use `pagehide`
- Speculation Rules `prefetch` (moderate) for in-site links; prerender only high-probability pages; never speculate side-effect URLs
- Fonts via `next/font` (fallback metrics + subsetting); `font-display: swap`

## Measure before and after

- `web-vitals/attribution` in prod; Lighthouse CI budget in CI; field p75 is the source of truth
- First-load diagnosis → `audit-performance`; implement instant nav → `enhance-web-instant-nav`
